Other notable third-party components (non-copyleft)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  - PostgreSQL and its contrib modules  --  PostgreSQL License
    (pg_trgm, pgcrypto, citext, hstore, ltree, pg_stat_statements, pageinspect,
    postgres_fdw, uuid-ossp, and the other contrib extensions listed in the
    manifests).
  - pgvector, pg_cron, pg_partman, pg_hint_plan, hll, pgaudit, hypopg, pg_repack,
    wal2json, prefix, ip4r, pgtap  --  PostgreSQL License / BSD / MIT / Apache-2.0
    (permissive; see each project for the exact terms).
  - pg_duckdb (analytics variant only)  --  MIT  (built from source; embeds
    DuckDB, MIT).  See docker/pg-duckdb-pkg/.
  - pg_stat_monitor (experimental variant only)  --  PostgreSQL License.
  - xatautils  --  Apache-2.0  (Xata's own extension, a fork of supautils;
    https://github.com/xataio/xata-utils). Built from source and installed as a
    prebuilt package. It hooks PostgreSQL core only; it is not combined with,
    and does not link against, PostGIS, pgRouting or any GPL/AGPL component.

Note on build-time script hardening: docker/custom-postgres/harden-ip4r-scripts.sh
adjusts the installed SQL scripts of the ip4r extension (schema-qualifying
built-in references). ip4r is permissively licensed; no copyleft component is
modified by this repository.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Obtaining source code
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

All copyleft components above are included unmodified from their upstream
binary distributions. The complete corresponding source code is available from:

  - PostgreSQL APT repository (PGDG):  https://apt.postgresql.org
    (source packages alongside the binary .deb packages used to build these
    images; versions match the pins in the extension manifests).
  - Debian archive:  https://deb.debian.org  and  https://snapshot.debian.org
    (for base-image and OS-package sources at the exact versions).
  - Upstream projects: PostGIS (https://git.osgeo.org/gitea/postgis/postgis),
    pgRouting (https://github.com/pgRouting/pgrouting), SFCGAL, CGAL and GEOS
    at the links above.

